{#
  Sold-count figure — the rounded «مباع +300 مرة» form. The Twig side of
  assets/js/partials/qissa-sold-count.js; change both together.

  The count is rounded down — to the ten under 100, to the hundred under
  1,000, to the thousand from there up — and printed with a "+" on the left of
  the digits, in Latin digits with a thousands comma:

         7  →  nothing (under 10 the line is not drawn)
        34  →  +30
       470  →  +400
     6,072  →  +6,000
    17,177  →  +17,000
   109,798  →  +109,000

  It rounds down, never up, so the "+" stays true. The zero groups and their
  commas are written out: after the rounding they are known in advance.

  Prints the figure only, inside <bdi> — that keeps the "+" on the number's
  left inside the Arabic sentence. The caller draws the icon and the words
  around it, so the caller checks `>= 10` as well.

  Params:
    count   int   a raw product.sold_quantity

  Used by: pages/product/single.twig, components/partials/qprod-card.twig,
  components/partials/qpack-card.twig.
#}
{%- set qsold = count|default(0) -%}
{%- if qsold >= 10 -%}
    {%- if qsold < 100 -%}
        {%- set qsold_label = '+' ~ (qsold // 10) ~ '0' -%}
    {%- elseif qsold < 1000 -%}
        {%- set qsold_label = '+' ~ (qsold // 100) ~ '00' -%}
    {%- elseif qsold < 1000000 -%}
        {%- set qsold_label = '+' ~ (qsold // 1000) ~ ',000' -%}
    {%- elseif qsold < 1000000000 -%}
        {#- a million and up: two groups before the zeros, the second padded to three digits -#}
        {%- set qsold_m = qsold // 1000000 -%}
        {%- set qsold_k = (qsold // 1000) - qsold_m * 1000 -%}
        {%- set qsold_label = '+' ~ qsold_m ~ ',' ~ (qsold_k < 10 ? '00' : (qsold_k < 100 ? '0' : '')) ~ qsold_k ~ ',000' -%}
    {%- else -%}
        {%- set qsold_label = qsold ~ '' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    <bdi>{{ qsold_label }}</bdi>
{%- endif -%}
